  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of selected enterprises in the foam sector provided the technical capacity to transition to Ozone Depleting Substance (ODS)-free technology

2. Number of technicians in the RAC sector provided the technical capacity and awareness for the purpose of transitioning towards low ODS and GWP technology</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in the foam sector lack the capacity to transition to Ozone Depleting Substance (ODS)-free technology (other than the support received from Stage-I)

2. RAC sector lacks the capacity to transition towards low ODS and low Global Warming Potential (GWP) alternatives (other than the support received from Stage-I)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Continue technology conversion for 55 SMEs (&lt;20MT HCFC consumption)

2. Procurement of equipment and tools to support ATC training programs on alternative refrigerant technology

3. Technical assistance workshops for Foam &amp; RAC sectors and engagement/awareness sessions for enforcement agencies/other stakeholders organized, in addition to continued capacity building through the e-CSTP programme

4. National ODS consumption allowable limit for Malaysia for 2020 = 335.24 ODP tonnes</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. As of 2021, the project has completed the conversion of 10 SMEs from Group 1, 2 SMEs from Group 2, while supporting 41 SMEs from Groups 1, 2, 3 and 4 in completing conversion by end of June 2022.

2. Provision of of RAC equipment to selected ATCs throughout the country. 

3. A total of 1,179 Service Technicians trained and certified under CSTP, and 68 enforcement officers trained on the control of use of HCFCs.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Continue technology conversion for 57 SMEs (&lt;20MT HCFC consumption)

2. Procurement of equipment and tools to support ATC training programs and DOE State enforcement offices

3. Technical assistance workshops for Foam &amp; RAC sectors and engagement/awareness sessions for enforcement agencies/other stakeholders organized, in addition to continued capacity building through the e-CSTP programme

4. National ODS consumption allowable limit for Malaysia for 2019 = 400 ODP tonnes</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
